      "review": {
        "upstream_changes": "Official signed stable 1.22.0 selected in the retained source review. All 30 XML sources and two installed legacy aliases preserved byte-for-byte. Five XML changes reviewed; pid_changed since floor 1 -> 8 is explicitly tested at negotiated versions 1,7,8,20.",
        "packaging_changes": "Authenticated Ubuntu 1.20.0-2 Debian archive; keep one Architecture: all Multi-Arch: foreign binary, original changelog history, install paths and metadata. Exact retained ECM 6.30.0-0supralinux3; upstream-required Qt CoreTools stays Ubuntu. Correct DEP-5 SPDX scopes, enable full native CTest suite.",
        "build_dependencies": "ECM >= 6.0 fulfilled by exact eligible milestone binary; CMake >=3.16, Ubuntu qt6-base-dev retained for ECM Qt6::qtpaths/CoreTools, Ubuntu Wayland >=1.24 SDK/scanner. No replacement Qt or Wayland runtime.",
        "test_policy": "All 120 upstream tests must execute in sbuild; upstream server-header tests call client-header and are preserved, so installed consumer separately generates/compiles all 30 true server headers, client headers and private-code objects. Baseline validates exact signed Ubuntu XML and installed CMake 1.20.0, compiles/runs a real private-socket client, records executable/header/code hashes and Qt/Wayland versions. After upgrade, unchanged Ubuntu client communicates with candidate server at versions 1,7,8,20; rebuilt candidate client does the same; exact 30 XML plus two aliases and CMake 1.22.0 are verified.",
